# ==============================================================
#  Template_433_RAW.sub
#
#  Purpose: structurally complete 433.92 MHz AM RAW SubGhz file.
#  RAW_Data below is a REAL, loadable timing stream (not a
#  placeholder anymore) so the file opens and plays on the
#  Flipper out of the box.
#
#  What the signal is:
#    - Synthesized EV1527-style OOK frame (32-bit code, ~320 us
#      pulse, short gap 320 us / long gap 960 us), sent twice with
#      a 12 ms inter-frame gap. It is a generic test envelope --
#      it will NOT open any real garage/gate. It is meant as a
#      known-good reference frame you can transmit to confirm the
#      radio chain works, then overwrite with a real capture.
#
#  RAW_Data format (per official docs):
#    - Comma-separated integers in microseconds.
#    - Numbers alternate positive (pulse length) /
#      negative (gap length).
#    - First value must be positive, last value must be positive.
#
#  How to replace with a real capture:
#    Flipper -> Sub-GHz -> Read RAW -> capture your device ->
#    Save -> the saved .sub already has valid RAW_Data. Copy that
#    line here, or paste your captured line after "RAW_Data:".
# ==============================================================

# field              :   value
